# 🎲 AETHERIA — RNG SYSTEM

> **Chance determines what appears.**
>
> **The Game State determines what actually happens.**
>
> **The Database remembers the result.**

The **RNG System** is the central probability and randomization system of Aetheria.

It provides controlled randomness for:

```text
Character Recruitment
Enemy Loot
Floor Rewards
Quest Rewards
Event Rewards
Item Drops
Special Rewards
```

The RNG System does **not** independently decide game progression.

Instead, it provides probability results to other systems.

---

# 📌 1. OVERVIEW

The RNG System acts as the core randomization engine.

```text
                         RNG SYSTEM
                              │
          ┌───────────────────┼───────────────────┐
          │                   │                   │
          ▼                   ▼                   ▼
    RECRUIT SYSTEM       LOOT SYSTEM        REWARD SYSTEM
          │                   │                   │
          ▼                   ▼                   ▼
     CHARACTER RNG        ITEM RNG          REWARD RNG
```

Additional systems:

```text
Quest System
Event System
Dungeon System
Tower System
Enemy System
```

can also request RNG results.

---

# 🎯 2. PURPOSE

The main purpose of the RNG System is to generate controlled random results.

Examples:

```text
Recruitment
→ Which Star?

Loot
→ Which Item?

Floor Reward
→ Which Reward?

Quest
→ Which Reward?

Enemy
→ What Drop?
```

The RNG System provides the probability calculation.

The system using RNG determines what the result means.

---

# 🧠 3. CORE PRINCIPLE

The RNG System follows:

> **RNG generates probability results, not game logic.**

For example:

```text
Recruit System
       ↓
Request RNG
       ↓
RNG System
       ↓
Star Result
       ↓
Recruit System
       ↓
Character Selection
```

The RNG System should not directly modify:

```text
Character
Inventory
Master
Quest
Floor
Database
```

Those changes are handled by the appropriate systems.

