# 🧠 43. RNG DOES NOT DECIDE OWNERSHIP

The RNG System should never directly assign ownership.

For example:

```text
RNG
 ↓
CHAR_000125
```

does not automatically mean:

```text
Master owns CHAR_000125
```

Instead:

```text
RNG
 ↓
Result
 ↓
Recruit System
 ↓
Game State System
 ↓
Ownership Update
 ↓
Database
```

This keeps responsibilities separated.

---

# 🔐 44. RNG INTEGRITY

The system must prevent:

```text
Invalid Pool
Invalid Star
Invalid Reward
Duplicate Character
Invalid Item
Negative Probability
Probability > 100%
Unauthorized RNG
Client-Side RNG Manipulation
```

---

# 📊 45. PROBABILITY VALIDATION

Every probability table must satisfy:

```text
Total Probability = 100%
```

Example:

```text
Gold Recruit

⭐       79%
⭐⭐      20%
⭐⭐⭐      1%

TOTAL = 100%
```

If:

```text
79 + 20 + 5 = 104%
```

the configuration is invalid.

---

# 🧪 46. RNG TESTING

The RNG System must support statistical testing.

Example:

```text
1,000,000 Rolls
```

Expected:

```text
⭐       ≈ 79%
⭐⭐      ≈ 20%
⭐⭐⭐      ≈ 1%
```

Actual results will naturally vary.

The purpose of testing is to verify that the distribution approximately follows the configured probability.

---

# 📈 47. BALANCE CONTROL

All probability values should be configurable.

Example:

```text
/recruit/gold.json
/recruit/ticket.json
/recruit/gem.json
/recruit/special.json
```

This allows balancing without changing the RNG engine itself.

